    <section class="card"><h2>2 / Learn a multiple from this snapshot</h2><p>${peers.length} token-recorded peers with positive market cap survive the same excluded category list and wrapped/staked/staking name screen. Deduplicate each category + CoinGecko ID (ticker fallback), keeping the largest TVL record to avoid counting versions repeatedly. Market cap is circulating, so this model does not claim FDV. Cross-category token reuse can remain; TVL is not revenue and curated assets can overlap.</p><div class="formula">rᵢ = observed token market capᵢ / protocol TVLᵢ<br>w = category peer count / (category peer count + 5)<br>M = clamp(exp(w × ln(category median r) + (1−w) × ln(global median r)), 0.05, 5)</div><p>The five-peer shrinkage strength and 0.05–5× bounds are assumptions. Sparse categories lean on the global median; with zero category peers, use the global median alone. Linear-interpolated quartiles and medians use every retained peer, not hand-picked names.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>3 / Value today's fundamentals, conditionally</h2><div class="formula">G = 1 + clamp(7-day TVL change, −50, 50) / 200<br>A = 0.65 + 0.35 × min(days tracked, 730) / 730<br>Implied cap = round(TVL × M × G × A × 0.70)</div><p>G is capped at 0.75–1.25×: a noisy weekly change should not determine the whole valuation. Missing growth gives 1×. Tracking maturity rewards a longer observed record; it does not establish launch date or years without a token. Unknown age gives an assumed 0.80×. The 30% transfer discount reflects missing rights, float and economics. These choices are explicitly assumed, not fitted outcomes.</p><p>Sensitivity low replaces the median with blended peer Q1 and multiplies by 0.5; high uses Q3 and 1.5. Other factors stay fixed. This is a stress range, not a statistical interval. Board rank sorts the base value descending, with slug as a deterministic tie-break.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>4 / Spend a budget, not a promise</h2><p>Every protocol receives a category-specific, chain-specific recipe. Use its first recorded chain as a planning convention; this is not proof of cheapest or native deployment. Assume a $200 pilot ceiling, or $0 for research/gated routes; actual supported assets, minimum tickets and access are unknown. Younger or unreported tracking age gives 60 days; otherwise 30. Reserve $40 Ethereum gas or $12 elsewhere, plus $8 for exchange/derivative/prediction routes. These are stop ceilings, not fee quotes. Opportunity cost assumes 5% annually.</p><p>The toy farm-share model assumes 5% of modeled circulating-cap value allocated over a 90-day season, proportional to pilot capital / (snapshot TVL + pilot capital) × active days / 90. It assumes immediate liquid rewards with no vesting and one eligible position. It is neither a real emission schedule nor an FDV allocation. Set eligibility to zero to see the loss of costs. Many pilots are uneconomic even under the positive scenario.</p></section>
